  "body": "See https://github.com/w3c/web-platform-tests/issues/5213. This requires abstracting setting cookies somehow.\r\n\r\nThere's an additional question around cookies about at which point they are actually set and synchronized across \"threads\". A logical place for synchronization would be when Fetch queues a task that the response is in (all headers that is; though what about synchronous?) or when WebSocket establishes the connection and queues a task for that (it currently lets HTML deal with that, but maybe Fetch should take ownership).",
